":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T09:28:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T09:28:14Z","body":"Can you ensure CPU particles work the same? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3611080153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3772902981","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630#issuecomment-3772902981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","id":3772902981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g4e5F","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T13:30:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T13:37:30Z","body":"I tested it on top of master and it does not fix the issue. Maybe something has changed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3772902981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3777255515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630#issuecomment-3777255515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","id":3777255515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hJFhb","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T10:12:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:12:05Z","body":"> I tested it on top of master and it does not fix the issue. Maybe something has changed.\r\n\r\nIn my tests this PR works (although I tested only the 2D particles). I have continuously emitting particles and this code:\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\n@onready var gpu_particles_2d: GPUParticles2D = $GPUParticles2D\r\n@onready var label: Label = $Label\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tgpu_particles_2d.finished.connect(func(): prints(\"FINISHED\"); label.text = \"FINISHED\")\r\n\r\nfunc _on_button_pressed() -> void:\r\n\tgpu_particles_2d.one_shot = true\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen the button is pressed, particles stop and the finished signal is emitted. But to be honest, this feels like a bandaid. When stopping the particles this way:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _on_button_2_pressed() -> void:\r\n\tgpu_particles_2d.emitting = false\r\n```\r\n\r\nthe finished signal is not emitted. Sure, the documentation says:\r\n\r\n> This signal is never emitted when [one_shot](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_gpuparticles2d.html#class-gpuparticles2d-property-one-shot) is disabled, as particles will be emitted and processed continuously.\r\n\r\nBut in my opinion this doesn't make any sense. Continuously emitting particles can be stopped by setting emitting to false and that works great, particles are no more generated and the particle effect is soon gone. Of course the finished signal should be emitted in this case too. I have had countless cases where this would make sense. For example, a car with exhaust gas particles. Continuously emitting particles until stopped by setting emitting = false and then doing something else when the particles stop, ie. using the finished signal.\r\n\r\nI would suggest a review for the decision that the finished signal is only emitted when one_shot = true and then doing a clean implementation based on that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3777255515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3777401076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630#issuecomment-3777401076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","id":3777401076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hJpD0","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T10:42:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:42:35Z","body":"> In my tests this PR works\r\n\r\nI used the MRP from linked issues (#93991 and #85802) for testing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3777401076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778581057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630#issuecomment-3778581057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","id":3778581057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hOJJB","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T14:59:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T14:59:53Z","body":"> I used the MRP from linked issues (#93991 and #85802) for testing.\r\n\r\nYou are correct. I tried the MRP from #93991 and it still fails. The MRP's code makes the \"mistake\" of setting `emitting = true` at the same time as setting `one_shot = true`. Without `emitting = true`, that MRP works with this PR. The problem with the current implementation of `GPUParticles2D` seems to be that it is neither known how all the stuff (emitting / one shot / restart / finished) should work nor how they actually do work. So when you want to stop particles and get finished signal, you just try stuff in random order until you get the desired result.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, this needs a proper redesign. A small fix, such as this PR was supposed to be, is not enough.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778581057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783563729","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630#issuecomment-3783563729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","id":3783563729,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hhJnR","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T10:08:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T10:08:23Z","body":"I agree. Oneshot has to go in favor of proper bursts. Unfortunately it's not something that is fast to do. But one day i want to have emission modes: continuous, bursts, emission by distance. Additionally, it should be easier to keyframe particles in Animation, and have proper playback/pause tools there.\r\n\r\nI don't see many paths forward other than leaving oneshot as-is and the finished() signal staying somewhat broken for now.\r\n\r\nThe workaround for this is to have your own way of tracking when particles are finished, especially for cases when oneshot is set after emitting (which imo should not be supported. you should just do `emitting = false; await timer (lifetime); do whatever;`).\r\nYou know when you want that behaviour, so it's much easier to write code with this context, than for particles to cover all possible usecases.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3783563729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]